      <h2 class="section__title">Socks Manufacturer FAQ</h2>
      
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order for custom socks?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            SDF Clothing offers a minimum order of 500 pairs per sock style. This MOQ applies to custom designs with your branding, colors, and specifications. For basic solid-color socks without customization, we can offer lower minimums. We provide flexible size and color combinations within the 500 pair minimum, allowing you to test designs without large commitment. For <a href="/low-moq-clothing-manufacturers">low MOQ clothing manufacturers</a>, our sock MOQ is competitive for custom production.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What fabrics are best for socks?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Cotton is the most common sock fabric, offering comfort, breathability, and moisture absorption. Combed cotton removes short fibers for smoother yarn. Bamboo provides natural antimicrobial properties and softness. Merino wool offers temperature regulation and odor resistance for performance socks. Synthetic blends (polyester, nylon, spandex) add durability and stretch. The best fabric depends on use - cotton for casual wear, merino wool for athletic performance, bamboo for sensitive skin. SDF sources all these materials for your sock production.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you print custom logos on socks?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, we offer custom logo printing on socks through several methods. Jacquard knitting weaves your logo directly into the sock fabric for permanent branding. Embroidery adds a stitched logo for premium appearance. Sublimation printing allows full-color designs on the sock surface. Screen printing works for simple logos on solid-color socks. The method depends on your design complexity, sock fabric, and budget. Jacquard knitting is most durable, while sublimation offers the most design flexibility. Our <a href="/printing-service">printing service</a> handles all logo application methods.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does sock manufacturing take?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Standard sock production takes 25-30 days from yarn sourcing to shipment. Sample development takes 7-10 days depending on design complexity. Simple solid-color socks may complete faster (20-25 days), while complex designs with multiple colors or custom logos may take 30-35 days. Sock production is generally faster than garment production due to simpler construction and specialized sock knitting machinery. Our <a href="/sampling-service">sampling service</a> ensures sample approval before bulk production. We provide clear timeline commitments.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do you manufacture athletic socks?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, SDF manufactures athletic socks for sports and performance applications. We produce running socks, basketball socks, soccer socks, and general athletic socks with performance features including moisture-wicking fibers, arch support, cushioned soles, and breathable mesh zones. Athletic socks often use synthetic blends with merino wool for temperature regulation and odor resistance. We can add custom branding and team colors for sports teams. Our athletic socks meet performance standards for durability and comfort.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you make bamboo socks?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, we manufacture bamboo socks using bamboo viscose fibers. Bamboo offers natural softness, moisture absorption, and antimicrobial properties that resist odor-causing bacteria. Bamboo socks are ideal for sensitive skin and eco-conscious consumers. We source certified bamboo from sustainable suppliers and can blend bamboo with cotton or spandex for improved durability and fit. Bamboo socks are particularly popular in the premium and sustainable sock markets. We can produce solid-color bamboo socks or custom designs with your branding.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What sizes do you manufacture?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            SDF manufactures socks in standard size ranges: S (US 4-6), M (US 7-9), L (US 10-12), XL (US 13-15). We also produce children's sizes (toddler, youth) and extended plus sizes upon request. Size grading in socks follows foot length measurements - each size increases by approximately 0.5-1 inch in foot length. We can develop custom size charts based on your target market's foot measurements. Specify your preferred size range in your product specifications.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you do private label sock packaging?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, we provide private label packaging for your socks. Options include custom branded polybags with your logo, cardboard header cards, hang tags, and retail-ready packaging. We can design packaging to match your brand identity and retail requirements. Private label packaging adds value and supports brand recognition at retail. Packaging costs vary by complexity and volume. For <a href=\"/private-label-manufacturer\">private label manufacturing</a>, we handle both product production and packaging to deliver retail-ready goods.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
